  "courseName": "Introductory Molecular Biology (200-level)",
  "estimatedLength": "40 minutes",
  "objectives": [
    "Identify the structural components of DNA (sugar-phosphate backbones, nitrogenous bases, and hydrogen bonds) and explain how they assemble into a double helix.",
    "Apply complementary base-pair rules (A\u2013T, G\u2013C) and relate hydrogen-bond number to base-pair identity (2 vs 3).",
    "Explain antiparallel strand orientation and how backbone directionality (5'\u21923') determines double-helix architecture.",
    "Trace DNA replication at the replication fork: helicase, single-strand binding proteins, DNA polymerase, and DNA ligase; map each enzyme\u2019s function.",
    "Explain why leading synthesis is continuous and lagging synthesis is discontinuous (Okazaki fragments) due to polymerase 5'\u21923' extension on antiparallel templates.",
    "Describe semiconservative replication and predict daughter-molecule strand composition after one and two rounds."
  ],
